    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nIs it possible to add a customizable highlight group for the current line in mini.files, similar to to the `MiniPickMatchCurrent` highlight group in mini.pick?\r\n\r\nSome colorschemes such as gruvbox use the same shade for both `CursorLine` and `NormalFloat`, and I'd rather not change my cursorline color everywhere else as a workaround.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/44929900/68a1baf4-a696-495b-abc3-ce08ad7c2669)",
